# Line endings for the files where they are load-bearing.
#
# Deliberately NOT a repo-wide `* text=auto`: most of this tree was written on
# Windows and renormalising all of it would produce a diff touching every file
# while fixing nothing. Only the files below actually break when their endings
# are wrong.

# The OpenAPI contract snapshot is regenerated and byte-compared in CI (see
# .github/workflows/ci.yml). Generated on Windows it carried CRLF, so the Linux
# runner rewrote all 8446 lines with LF and failed the gate on a file whose
# content had not changed. `scripts/dump_openapi_snapshot.py` writes LF for the
# same reason; this is the half that survives a checkout.
docs/openapi.json text eol=lf

# These run on Linux - the board and the container. A shell script that reaches
# the box with CRLF fails as `bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M`, which reads like a
# missing shell rather than a line-ending problem. They are all LF today; this
# keeps an edit from a Windows editor from silently changing that.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
